<div class="editorial-layout"><div class="chapter-list"><details class="plan-chapter" id="project-detail-1" open><summary><span class="chapter-count">01</span><h3>The plan for your space</h3>
<span aria-hidden="true" class="chapter-toggle">+</span></summary><div class="chapter-body prose"><p>Arvada’s soil works against a traditional lawn before the summer heat even gets involved. Much of the city sits on heavy clay, the kind that bakes hard and cracks in July and turns to soup after a spring storm. Add Colorado’s intense sun and thin rainfall on top of that, and it’s no surprise so many Arvada lawns look tired by June. Xeriscape landscaping services take a different approach, working with what the soil and climate actually offer instead of fighting them every season.</p>

<p>Ridgewell Landscape and Design has spent over a decade building landscapes across the Denver metro, and Arvada’s particular mix of clay soil, sun exposure, and neighborhood age is something we plan around from the first site visit.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details class="plan-chapter" id="project-detail-2"><summary><span class="chapter-count">02</span><h3>What Do Xeriscape Landscaping Services Actually Include?</h3>
<span aria-hidden="true" class="chapter-toggle">+</span></summary><div class="chapter-body prose"><p>A full xeriscape landscaping service covers more than swapping grass for gravel. It typically means assessing your soil, redesigning irrigation around drip lines instead of broad spray, selecting native and drought-adapted plants, and grading the yard so water goes where plants need it rather than running off into the street. Done well, the result is a yard that needs a fraction of the water a traditional lawn does, while still looking full and colorful through spring, summer, and fall.</p>

<p>One quick clarification, since it comes up often. A yard with mostly rock and a few scattered succulents is closer to what people call “zeroscaping,” which is not the same thing. A properly built xeriscape is densely planted and can look just as lush as a traditional garden.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details class="plan-chapter" id="project-detail-3"><summary><span class="chapter-count">03</span><h3>Why Arvada’s Clay Soil Changes the Approach</h3>
<span aria-hidden="true" class="chapter-toggle">+</span></summary><div class="chapter-body prose"><p>Clay soil holds water differently than sandy or loamy soil, and that matters more for xeriscaping than most homeowners expect. Clay tends to drain slowly, then crack and shed water quickly once it dries out, which is part of why so many Arvada lawns either sit soggy after watering or bake hard within a few days. A xeriscape design built for Arvada needs soil amendments and plant choices that actually tolerate this specific soil type, not a generic plant list pulled from a different climate.</p>

<p>The City of Arvada has also been paying attention to water use at a municipal level. Arvada’s Water Saving Programs, run in partnership with Resource Central, give residents access to lawn replacement support, free sprinkler evaluations, and waterwise yard seminars. The city’s Parks Department has gone a step further, converting sections of public parkland, including an expanded turf conversion project at Tennyson Knolls Park, from thirsty bluegrass to lower-water native grasses.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details class="plan-chapter" id="project-detail-4"><summary><span class="chapter-count">04</span><h3>Our Xeriscape Landscaping Services in Arvada</h3>
<span aria-hidden="true" class="chapter-toggle">+</span></summary><div class="chapter-body prose"><h3><strong>Site and Soil Assessment</strong></h3>

<p>We start every Arvada project by evaluating the specific soil conditions on your property, since clay content can vary block by block, and even yard to yard. This step shapes everything that follows, from drainage design to which plants actually have a chance of thriving.</p>

<h3><strong>Xeriscape Design</strong></h3>

<p>From there, we build a plan around native and adapted plants suited to both Arvada’s climate and its clay, arranged for color and texture across multiple seasons rather than one short bloom window.</p>

<h3><strong>Lawn-to-Xeriscape Conversion</strong></h3>

<p>Most projects start with removing an existing lawn that isn’t earning its water bill anymore. We remove the turf, amend the clay soil underneath where needed, and rebuild the space around efficient drip irrigation.</p>

<h3><strong>Installation and Maintenance</strong></h3>

<p>Grading, irrigation lines, hardscape elements, and planting are handled directly by our team, usually led personally by co-founder Francisco Garcia and lead designer Chris. Once installed, we offer ongoing maintenance while your plants establish over their first year or two.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details class="plan-chapter" id="project-detail-5"><summary><span class="chapter-count">05</span><h3>Signs You Could Benefit from Xeriscape Landscaping Services</h3>
<span aria-hidden="true" class="chapter-toggle">+</span></summary><div class="chapter-body prose"><ul>
<li>Your lawn pools water after rain, then cracks and dries within days</li>
<li>You’re in a newer development like Candelas where the soil was heavily disturbed during construction</li>
<li>You’re in an older neighborhood like Ralston Valley or Lake Arbor where the original grass has never really thrived</li>
<li>Mowing a sloped section of your yard feels more like erosion control than lawn care</li>
<li>Your water bill jumps noticeably the moment sprinkler season starts</li>
</ul>
</div>
</details>
<details class="plan-chapter" id="project-detail-6"><summary><span class="chapter-count">06</span><h3>Water Conservation Support Available to Arvada Residents</h3>
<span aria-hidden="true" class="chapter-toggle">+</span></summary><div class="chapter-body prose"><p>Arvada residents can access water-saving support through the city’s partnership programs, which help offset part of the cost of a lawn replacement project. Program terms and availability shift over time, so we recommend confirming current details directly, and our team can point you toward what’s currently offered when we prepare your estimate.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details class="plan-chapter" id="project-detail-7"><summary><span class="chapter-count">07</span><h3>Why Arvada Homeowners Choose Ridgewell for Xeriscape Landscaping Services</h3>
<span aria-hidden="true" class="chapter-toggle">+</span></summary><div class="chapter-body prose"><p>Founded in 2011 by longtime Colorado resident Francisco Garcia, Ridgewell Landscape and Design has spent over a decade learning what actually works in this region’s soil and climate, Arvada’s clay included. We’re licensed and insured throughout Colorado and hold a perfect 5.0-star rating on Google, built through finished projects. Because our team stays small, Francisco and Chris are personally involved in most jobs from design through the final walkthrough.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details class="plan-chapter" id="project-detail-8"><summary><span class="chapter-count">08</span><h3>Get Your Free Xeriscape Landscaping Estimate in Arvada</h3>
<span aria-hidden="true" class="chapter-toggle">+</span></summary><div class="chapter-body prose"><p>If your lawn is fighting Arvada’s soil and losing, let’s talk about a design that works with it instead.<a href="/contact/"> Get Your Free Estimate</a> and our team will follow up to discuss your yard.</p>

<hr/></div>
</details>
<details class="plan-chapter" id="project-detail-9"><summary><span class="chapter-count">09</span><h3>Your questions, answered</h3>
<span aria-hidden="true" class="chapter-toggle">+</span></summary><div class="chapter-body prose"><h3><strong> How does Arvada’s clay soil affect a xeriscape conversion?</strong> </h3>

<p>A clay soil drains slowly and then cracks once it dries, which makes plant selection and soil amendment more important in Arvada than in areas with sandier soil. A design built specifically around your yard’s soil conditions has a much better chance of establishing successfully than a generic plant list.</p>

<h3><strong>Is xeriscaping the same as a rock garden?</strong> </h3>

<p>No. A rock-heavy yard with few plants is closer to what’s sometimes called “zeroscaping.” A true xeriscape is fully planted and can look just as full and colorful as a traditional garden, using plants selected for low water needs instead of large expanses of bare rock.</p>

<h3><strong> Does the City of Arvada help residents with lawn replacement costs?</strong> </h3>

<p>Arvada offers water-saving support through partnership programs that can help with parts of a lawn replacement project, including free sprinkler evaluations and waterwise yard seminars. Program details change periodically, so it’s worth confirming current terms, and we can help point you in the right direction during your estimate.</p>

<h3><strong> Can I convert just part of my yard instead of the whole thing?</strong> </h3>

<p>Yes. Many Arvada homeowners start with a problem area, like a strip along the driveway or a sloped section where grass never grows well, and expand later if they choose. A partial conversion is a common and reasonable way to start.</p>

<h3><strong>How long before a new xeriscape looks fully filled in?</strong> </h3>

<p>Most plantings need one to two growing seasons to fully establish their root systems and reach their mature size. The yard will look good on installation day, but the fullest, most established look typically develops over the following year or two.</p>
</div>
</details>
